course_details.Learning Objectives:
By the end of this course, you should be able to:
1. understand, compare, and assess the various meanings of infrastructure;
2. formulate and respond to theoretical questions about knowledge, displacement, and development in terms of construction and demolition;
3. apply concepts and approaches discussed in class and readings to real life cases and contexts;
4. develop informed positions on different issues that pertain to global infrastructure practices;
5. understand the different ways that social scientists, in particular sociologists, have methodologically approached the study of infrastructure.
